<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41336" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιτηδ-ειότης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fitness, suitableness, convenience</i> for a purpose,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				27
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					778a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				1p.9U.
			</span></i>(pl.) : <i>tendency, liability,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theon Gymn.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.208
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πρὸς πόλεμον</span> all
			<i>material,</i> etc., for carrying on war, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.23.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>requirement,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵνα πρὸς ἑκάστην ἐ. τὸ προσῆκον
					γένηται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>Tact.</u>
					35.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>friendliness, kindness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἅπαντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					1.112J.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
